Model-to-Deployment Selection Rules

For each model and deployment type number 3 through 7, select the best matching tag/recommendation row.

Selection must be deterministic.

Recommended ranking:

1. Prefer assessments in this order:
  • recommended
  • full_gpu_fit
  • cpu_only_practical
  • partial_gpu_offload
  • runs_with_constraints
  • cloud_only
  • unknown
  • insufficient_memory
2. Prefer the model default tag when tied.
3. Prefer smaller installed storage when tied.
4. Prefer stable lexical tag_id when still tied.

If a model has no valid row for a deployment type, do not silently omit the deployment type from the model README table. Mark it as unavailable in model.json and the README table. Only create the numbered folder when there is a selected row with enough identity to produce a truthful info.json.

Slug Rules

Slugs must be stable and filesystem-safe:

• lowercase
• spaces become -
• /, :, and unsafe punctuation become -
• collapse repeated dashes
• trim leading/trailing dashes
• never produce an empty slug

If two source records would produce the same slug, append a stable short hash or source ID suffix.

