Validation Command

Add either a CLI subcommand or script that validates the generated page tree.

Recommended CLI:

```text
eight-ball validate-pages
```

Minimum checks:

• generated pages root exists
• 02-models does not exist
• family page count > 0
• deployment type page count is exactly 5
• model page count > 0
• numbered model deployment page count > 0
• install manifest exists
• install manifest parses
• every manifest model deployment points to an existing info.json
• every deployment type ID is one of 3, 4, 5, 6, 7

8.2 Installer Contract

After C5, 8.2 should use the generated manifest as the source of truth.

The installer selection flow should be:

1. Detect hardware.
2. Convert hardware into deployment type number 3 through 7.
3. Resolve requested model ID or model alias.
4. Read data/generated/pages/install-manifest.json.
5. Select manifest.models[model_id].deployments[deployment_type_id].
6. If unavailable, fall back to the next smaller/suitable deployment type or tag.
7. Pull/run the selected ollama_identifier.
8. Log both selected model and deployment type.

8.2 must record:

• detected CPU threads
• detected RAM
• detected GPU name, if any
• detected VRAM, if any
• selected deployment type ID
• selected model ID
• selected tag ID
• selected Ollama identifier
• fallback reason, if fallback occurred

